WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.430
An appointment reminder.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.870
A shorter email. A
checklist from your notes.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.710
That's where to start with Claude:

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.750
a small job you already know how to check.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.790
Every business in this course is invented.

6
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.910
A Hamilton accountancy,
a Christchurch builder,

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.790
a Wellington HR team.

8
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.270
So no real client
information goes into a chat.

9
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.270
Claude is Anthropic's AI assistant.

10
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.590
Free is enough for these exercises.

11
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.710
Pro and Max are individual subscriptions.

12
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.150
Team and Enterprise are
plans for organisations.

13
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.950
If your workplace has approved an account,

14
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.190
use that one, and check which
workspace you're in before you type.

15
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.070
A personal account on a work email doesn't
automatically become a Team account.

16
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.990
Free and paid plans can
both have usage limits.

17
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.070
Long messages, attachments and
long conversations use more,

18
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.030
so keep practice chats short and focused.

19
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.670
Next, privacy. On a personal account,

20
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.230
open Settings, then Privacy.

21
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.950
Find Help improve our AI models,

22
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.350
and switch it off for this practice.

23
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.390
Be clear about what that switch does.

24
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.670
It controls whether your
chats help improve the models.

25
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.670
It doesn't make private business
information safe to paste in.

26
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.070
Organisation accounts
have different data terms,

27
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.990
so check your team's rules.

28
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.190
And if you're unsure about permission,

29
00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.350
pause the real task, and keep
practising with the invented example.

30
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.630
Now the job. Our invented Hamilton
accountancy needs an email for a client

31
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.310
coming to an appointment.

32
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.110
Ask for a warm message
in New Zealand English,

33
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.310
with a subject line,
in under ninety words.

34
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:50.590
Give only the facts it needs:
bring last year's accounts,

35
00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.230
and a list of questions.

36
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.830
Keep the appointment date as a
placeholder in square brackets.

37
00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.270
And say: don't add deadlines or fees.

38
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.230
Then read the draft beside your notes.

39
00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.070
Here's the catch. It's friendly and tidy,

40
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.430
but it's added a reply-by deadline,

41
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.710
and a fee. Your notes
never mentioned either.

42
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.910
So take them out. Anything you didn't
supply doesn't belong in the message.

43
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.150
A warmer tone only helps when it
keeps the meaning of your notes.

44
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.870
Note what you changed, then have a
person approve it before it's sent.

45
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.230
That note helps you explain the draft,

46
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.630
and repeat the exercise next time.

47
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.230
Choose something small enough
to review in a few minutes.

48
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.550
A reminder works well, because you can
compare every detail with a short set of

49
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.800
notes.

50
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.790
So, your first step.

51
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.830
Know your account. Check Privacy.

52
00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.910
Choose one safe task, and
finish with one reviewed draft.

53
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.030
This is independent training by The Colab,

54
00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.270
not an Anthropic certification.

55
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.390
Open the first text
lesson, and get set up.
